A||||6||286SE'S||Sunbird Headlight Motors||||14||
Z||000000||286SE'S||08-08-2000||02:01 PM||||There was this sunbird GT with motorized "eyelids" on the headlights at the junkyard and I remember reading that the headlight motors were the same as 87-88 Fieros. Motors were the same and I pulled the "guide" module then noticed that the wiring harness for the lights was easily accessable. 10 minutes later I had the whole system, 2 motors, controller and uncut wiring. $35.00 and I am all ready for a Fiero motor upgrade without having to pull the old relay system out or creating problems with fan/turn signal wiring. Funny they put these same motors on these little half covers!<BR>Terry||||reg||14
Z||000001||HugGRRRFiero||08-08-2000||02:32 PM||||   Cool, so the motors plugged right in to the Fiero harness plugs?  You said you took the whole harness out of the sunbird, did you have to use any of it to get them to work?  <P>   You guys may already know this, but I believe 80's firebird and trans am headlight motors work too.  The left motor on the firebird goes on the right on the Fiero and vice a versa.<P>Brent<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/huggrrr.gif"> <BR> <A HREF="mailto:HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com">HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||14
Z||000002||Monkeyman||08-09-2000||02:21 AM||||HugGRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRR--The T/A motors only work on the old style headlight system (pre-'87).||||reg||1
Z||000003||HugGRRRFiero||08-09-2000||07:55 AM|||| Yep. pre-87's is what I meant by 80's.  Thanks Monkeyman.<P> Brent<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/huggrrr.gif"> <BR> <A HREF="mailto:HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com">HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||286SE'S||08-09-2000||11:04 AM||||What I am suggesting is to avoid a lot of extra work by adding just the newer motor circuit. The sunbird harness doesn't just plug into the Fiero harness. The input side is still spliced in. The part that I am talking about is the wiring from the controller "GUIDE" box to the headlight motors. The 87-88 Fiero harness is part of the turn-signals/fan motor/headlight bulbs.<BR>Leave this all alone and run just the motor wiring next to it. The input to the "GUIDE' box is still spliced. Two red wires for the fusable links, a black ground and the yellow and white on/off wires from the headlight switch.<BR>Previous posts suggested pulling all the front wiring harness from the doner car and putting it in yours. I just don't want to create any electrical problems by doing that.<P>Now back to the Trans-AM motors, I see the same two kinds, 82-86 "relay" models and 87-92 "GUIDE" models. Lets get this straight:<BR>TransAm 87 and newer are NOT the same as Fiero 87-88? (They sure look the same, Holding one of each right now. part number is just a few digits off. Yes, left is right)<BR>AND<BR>The older relay motors, pre 87, are exactly the same as 84-96 Fiero and do work? <BR>Any response would be appreciated, Thanks<BR>Terry<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Monkeyman||08-09-2000||11:23 AM||||The way I understand previous threads, the "older" style T/A motors will work with the "older" style Fiero motors (switched, of course).  I don't know anything about the newer ones.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Raydar||08-09-2000||01:36 PM||||I've also heard that the late 80s Firebird headlight motors can be substituted for the 87-88 Fiero. (Swapped left to right.)<P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR>88 Formula T-Top <BR>88 Coupe (ISO big V-6)<P>When I die, I want to go peacefully, in my sleep, like Grandpa.<BR>Not screaming, like the passengers in his car.||||reg||1
